# Enterprise Customer Engagement (ECE) — Platform Constitution

Status: **ENTERPRISE APPROVED** · Frozen · Canonical customer self-service projection  
Sprint foundation: **CO-BIZ-004**

## Constitutional principles

1. The customer portal is a **projection** of existing enterprise services — not a second operating system.
2. **Consume:** Enterprise Deal Lifecycle · ETE · Document Registry / Document Requests · EDC · ENCE · (optional) EBI.
3. **Never** invent a customer workflow engine, duplicate status tracking, or parallel task ownership.
4. Customer-facing tasks are **allowlisted projections** of ETE + Document Requests LOD — ETE remains the sole task SSOT.
5. Document storage remains **Enterprise Document Registry** (CO-DOC-002 ingestion channel).
6. Auth for Phase 1–6 stays **opaque upload/engagement tokens** — do not expose Opportunity IDs or mount under ERP `(dashboard)`.

## SSOT paths

| Concern | Path |
|---------|------|
| Compose / projection | `src/lib/enterprise-customer-engagement/` |
| Types | `src/types/enterprise-customer-engagement.ts` |
| Portal UI | `/customer-engagement/[token]` · Documents via `/document-upload/[token]` |
| CX Score | `deriveCustomerExperienceScore` (single formula) |
| Docs | `docs/co-biz-004/CO-BIZ-004-CUSTOMER-ENGAGEMENT-READINESS-REPORT.md` |

## Forbidden

- Parallel customer task / reminder / stage engines  
- Writing customer portal state back as a competing Deal / Opportunity ownership store  
- Showing internal ETE work types (Lender Call, Internal Review, etc.) to customers  
- Mounting customer self-service under Administration or employee dashboard chrome  

